      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The game already does that, only once the world creator pushes an update to their world you'll need to download it again. Not sure if avatars function the same but I assume they do as they arguably use more drive space and bandwidth.\n\nHere's an idea though: Do you have any of those \"PC Optimizer\" programs like CCleaner for example? IIRC they often delete temporary data and vrchat downloads the worlds into those folders and it might just happen that those programs delete the data every time you run that program without you realizing it. \n\nAnd spoilers, these programs don't make your PC faster anyway so if that's your goal stop using them.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
